From 85516b7ab3c9509d3aa53971218ee889fd8b296d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominick Morales <dmorales2024@my.fit.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:00:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] KVM: x86: introspection events and page access tracking

CR0/CR3/CR4, MSR, CPUID, XSETBV, hypercall and trap events, register and
XSAVE access, exception injection, and single-step completion reported
through the request loop so it never runs inside the emulator.

Page access: restricted gfns are emulated (never mapped when read is
taken away, W/X stripped in make_spte otherwise, no huge pages over
them), and the emulator reports reads, writes, fetches and cmpxchg
before doing them. A vetoed access returns EMULATION_RETRY_INSTR.

Based on the Bitdefender KVMI patches (kvmi-v7, kvmi-v12).
